Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?comms:=20JMAP=20fix=20=E2=80=94=20accept=20'jma?=
 =?UTF-8?q?p'=20in=20EmailService=20constructor=20(NoSuchProviderException?=
 =?UTF-8?q?)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Runtime crash on device: account failed with 'NoSuchProviderException: jmap'.
The constructor's protocol dispatch (pop3/imap/smtp property branches) threw
for any other protocol at the else — batch 2 only wired jmap into connect()'s
dispatch, so JmapSync.monitor's  died before connecting (the config-UI path never constructed EmailService
with protocol=jmap, which is why activation looked OK). Add a no-op jmap
branch: JMAP is not a Jakarta provider; no session properties apply.
---
 app/src/main/java/eu/faircode/email/EmailService.java | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/eu/faircode/email/EmailService.java b/app/src/main/java/eu/faircode/email/EmailService.java
index abdfd6af8b..3b4ab91553 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/eu/faircode/email/EmailService.java
+++ b/app/src/main/java/eu/faircode/email/EmailService.java
@@ -334,6 +334,13 @@ public class EmailService implements AutoCloseable {
 
             properties.put("mail." + protocol + ".auth", "true");
 
+        } else if ("jmap".equals(protocol)) {
+            // comms: JMAP is NOT a Jakarta provider — it runs on the parallel
+            // JmapService field (see connect()'s dispatch). No Jakarta session
+            // properties apply; constructing must simply not throw. Without
+            // this branch, JmapSync.monitor's `new EmailService(account,…)`
+            // died with NoSuchProviderException: jmap before ever connecting.
+
         } else
             throw new NoSuchProviderException(protocol);
     }
